0..77 Comment "// Definitions a Rust caller runs on its own values, and a Rust function they"
78..86 Comment "// call."
87..89 Comment "//"
90..168 Comment "// The first direction: Rust holds the composed program and calls a definition"
169..247 Comment "// by name. The second: the `extern` block declares the Rust caller\'s `add` as"
248..325 Comment "// an operation of the interface `Boundary`, and `quadrupled` performs it. No"
326..401 Comment "// handler here answers it, so the run offers it to the Rust caller\'s host,"
402..480 Comment "// which calls its own `add`. Nothing crosses by layout yet: each argument and"
481..550 Comment "// answer is a value the runtime holds as itself, a `u32` as a `u32`."
551..553 Comment "//"
554..630 Comment "// The Rust test composes this source, names each definition and calls it on"
631..708 Comment "// values it builds, then reads the answer back. Each `runs` item below makes"
709..786 Comment "// the same call from gandr, so both sides state one answer. `quadrupled` has"
787..842 Comment "// none, since only the Rust caller answers `Boundary`."
843..845 Comment "//"
846..924 Comment "// - see: #2901 — not implemented: values crossing by Rust\'s default layout,"
925..987 Comment "//   and the block\'s function row admitted when it is declared"
988..1063 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/boundary.rs` — the Rust caller"
1064..1141 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/function-row.gandr` — the function row an"
1142..1175 Comment "//   `extern` is admitted against"
